-- found by the rows (2026-09-15): a draft is a word from a person to themself. jordan's "Photography — draft" is
-- addressed to jordan, so it is human-to-human and off everyone else's audience, and the remainder rule as HERE.md
-- piece 4 writes it ("author a human presence, every address a human presence") narrates "jordan wrote to jordan" to
-- the whole room. the assay keeps the rule as written (mayaHears, sofiaHears, lindaHears all carry shape invJ) so the
-- row parts the day the rule is sharpened. the sharpening is the couple's and the maintainer's: a self-addressed word
-- leaves no remainder (the author is the whole audience), or a draft is not a message until sent (one-hop.sql's own
-- reading: "a note to himself until he sends it").
-- held (waiting on: the maintainer's word on a word to oneself)
